alse,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T14:01:40+00:00","id":"hr563-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-20","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-20","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"563","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001115","district":27,"fullName":"Rep. Cloud, Michael [R-TX-27]","party":"R","state":"TX"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-20","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>No Retaining Every Gun In a System That Restricts Your Rights Act</strong></p><p>This bill modifies the retention requirements for firearm transaction records of federal firearms licensees (FFLs) that go out of business.</p><p>Current law generally requires FFLs that go out of business to deliver their firearm transaction records to the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives (ATF).</p><p>This bill removes the requirement for FFLs that go out of business to deliver their firearm transaction records to the ATF. Further, the bill requires the ATF to destroy all out-of-business records it has collected from FFLs.</p>","updateDate":"2025-03-17T19:27:04Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"No Retaining Every Gun In a System That Restricts Your Rights Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:20:38Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:20:38Z"}
